		<item>
			<title>In Memory of Namgyal Sherpa</title>
			<link>http://www.everestpeaceproject.org/news/news/274-namgyalsherpa.html</link>
			<guid>http://www.everestpeaceproject.org/news/news/274-namgyalsherpa.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<p><img src="http://www.everestpeaceproject.org/images/stories/news/namgyal_sherpa_summiteverestmed.jpg" border="0" alt="Namgyal Sherpa" title="Namgyal Sherpa" width="300" /><br /><br />May 17th, 2013:<br />I cannot believe that I have to write these words...but my friend Namgyal Sherpa died on Mt. Everest yesterday. I still do not believe it. When my friend DaYula Sherpa contacted me yesterday via Facebook messenger and told me that he had heard that Namgyal had died on Everest - I told him impossible. Not Namgyal. Namgyal is an incredible climber; he is strong; and this was to be the 10th summit of the mountain. <br /> <br /> Impossible.</p>
]]></description>
			<author>lancetrumbull@gmail.com (Administrator)</author>
			<category>Latest</category>
			<pubDate>Sat, 18 May 2013 01:40:15 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Everest Children's Book Now Available</title>
			<link>http://www.everestpeaceproject.org/news/news/273-everest-childrens-book-now-available.html</link>
			<guid>http://www.everestpeaceproject.org/news/news/273-everest-childrens-book-now-available.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<p><img src="http://www.everestpeaceproject.org/images/stories/news/everest_beauty_cover_websitesml.jpg" border="0" align="left" /></p>
<p>August 2012:<br />Everest: A Climb for Peace - A Children's Book is now available in Paperback and eBook editions!</p>
<div id="_mcePaste" style="position: absolute; left: -10000px; top: 0px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden;">Everest: A Climb for Peace - A Children's Book is now available in Paperback and eBook editions!</div>
<div id="_mcePaste" style="position: absolute; left: -10000px; top: 0px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden;">- The book chronicles the inspirational journey of 'Peace Climbers' from different faiths and cultures as they climb to the summit of the tallest mountain in the world. The focus is on Palestinian Ali Bushnaq and Israeli's Dudu Yifrah and Micha Yaniv.</div>
<div id="_mcePaste" style="position: absolute; left: -10000px; top: 0px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden;">They attempt to set aside their differences to create a path of teamwork, friendship and cooperation to try to summit the world’s highest peak. This however, is easier said than done. Their nations have been fighting for many years - will three men also fight or will they unite and make it together to the summit? Follow them as they climb the tallest mountain in the world.</div>
<div id="_mcePaste" style="position: absolute; left: -10000px; top: 0px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden;">Click Here to Order a Copy Today - Paperback and eBook Versions Available</div>
<p>- The book chronicles the inspirational journey of 'Peace Climbers' from different faiths and cultures as they climb to the summit of the tallest mountain in the world. The focus is on Palestinian Ali Bushnaq and Israeli's Dudu Yifrah and Micha Yaniv.</p>
<p>{sharethis}</p>
<ul>
</ul>
]]></description>
			<author>lancetrumbull@gmail.com (Administrator)</author>
			<category>Latest</category>
			<pubDate>Sat, 25 Aug 2012 17:06:33 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Everest and PBS stations update - July 2012</title>
			<link>http://www.everestpeaceproject.org/news/news/270-everest-and-pbs-stations-update-july-2012.html</link>
			<guid>http://www.everestpeaceproject.org/news/news/270-everest-and-pbs-stations-update-july-2012.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<p><img src="http://www.everestpeaceproject.org/images/stories/eppfilm/epp_dvdcover_med.jpg" border="0" alt="Everest: A Climb for Peace - Narrated by Orlando Bloom" title="Everest: A Climb for Peace - Narrated by Orlando Bloom" align="left" /></p>
<p>Updated! Everest July 2012: A Climb for Peace continues its airings on National PBS Stations across the US.<br /> Amazing news: Originally we were thinking that the film would be seen on 25 stations and hopefully be shown perhaps 100 times over the course of the 3 year period. Well, as of today the film has been shown 3183 times on 339 stations in 47 states with a 86% coverage! And we still have 16 more months of screenings - incredible! <br /><br /><span style="color: #800000;"><strong>- Call Your Local PBS Station to find out when the film is showing next in your area</strong>!</span></p>
<p>{sharethis}</p>
<ul>
</ul>
]]></description>
			<author>lancetrumbull@gmail.com (Administrator)</author>
			<category>Latest</category>
			<pubDate>Sat, 21 Jul 2012 15:49:55 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
